WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.100
Reccoa's Shadow

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:52.210
- How long now?!
- We've caught up with the Audhumla!

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.940
We'll make contact in about five minutes!

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.880
Okay, send out our mobile suits.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.480
I'm going out, too!

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.190
This is no longer Dakar.
I'll do as I wish!

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.390
Is there anything left to be loaded...

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.820
...Lieutenant Quattro?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.760
Kamille's doing it for me.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.820
Oh...!

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.330
Sorry to cause you all the trouble,
Director Hayato.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.890
Not a problem.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:22.070
The general public gets easily excited
but calms down just as fast.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.840
Please proceed quickly with the operation.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.710
I was told the same thing by Beltorchika.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.810
You were?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.480
Well, we Oldtypes can't help giving
unnecessary advice.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.010
Actually, it's probably an accurate
assessment of human nature.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.990
And it is your job to change
that characteristic in people.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.160
No, Director Hayato, it is <i>our</i> job.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.030
I stand corrected.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.210
Will the Argama come for us?

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.370
They can't come down low enough.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.170
At least, that's what we should assume.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.740
But then...!

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.210
We'll wait for the Argama in orbit.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.940
Thanks to the Minovsky particles...

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.220
...it's impossible to target
a small shuttle from the Earth's surface.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.720
Right.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.690
It looks like you're ready.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.590
The sooner you leave, the better.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.890
It's not as if the Titans
have given up on their attack.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.490
You're right.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.620
Amuro, take care of
everything else for me.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.500
Beltorchika says you're more handsome
without the sunglasses.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.170
Please leave everything here
on Earth to us...

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:30.910
...Char Aznable.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.210
You've changed, Amuro.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.940
You've returned to the Amuro Ray
of the old days.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.380
You're the one who changed me.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.920
Well...!

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.580
It's from the bridge.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:48.960
What?!

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.360
How many enemy mobile suits?

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.400
Amuro!

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.730
We'll cover the shuttle's take-off.
We won't let the enemy get in the way.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.930
Thanks, Amuro!

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.670
Launch the shuttle!

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.270
Please take me to the gun turret.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.670
Kamille, come!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.110
We still have time.
We should fight, too!

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.050
Our duties here on Earth are over.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.520
Our immediate duty
is to return to space uninjured.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:15.790
Yes, sir.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.010
It's that guy! Why haven't the Zeta
and the Hyaku Shiki come out yet?!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.520
It's the new model from yesterday.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.280
All mobile suits!
We'll hold the enemy here!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.830
Audhumla! Ascend!

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.830
Shuttle positioning for launch.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.860
Okay!

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.400
It's started.
Are you okay with the controls, sir?

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.940
I've had training on this.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.340
I suggest you also learn
how to pilot a shuttle.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.470
I already can.
I flew one, don't you remember?

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.150
No, I mean learning to operate
one in the official way.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:20.850
Self-taught style isn't good enough.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:24.690
I'll learn when it becomes more peaceful,
Char Azna...!

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.350
You can still call me
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.430
Yes, Lieutenant Quattro.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.400
It's what's left of the Titans' force.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.700
Go down!

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.740
Why aren't you coming out, Zeta Gundam?!

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.610
I get it!

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.150
They're trying to get away!

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.190
Melord!

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.750
Attack the Audhumla!
Even if it means ramming into it!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.660
He says ram into the enemy.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.290
He can't be sane.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.800
He's only telling us to be prepared,
that's all!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.400
Fire missiles!

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.280
We'll see who gives up first!
Fire everything we have!

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.320
We're doing it!

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.050
Time it with the enemy's movements!

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.750
You'll never hit them
by firing randomly!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.750
There's one!
It's close!

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.730
Fall! Fall! Fall!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.770
Lieutenant, we should launch
to make the Audhumla lighter!

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.960
We haven't received orders
to take off from Hayato yet!

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.630
But...!

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.140
Close your eyes if you're scared!

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.170
Hayato! Launch the shuttle!

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.840
While I'm shooting down
the enemy Garuda!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.280
I did it!

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.300
I'm launching the shuttle! Ready?!

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.120
<i>We're ready! We'll follow your orders!</i>

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.200
<i>Director Hayato, any message for Katz?</i>

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:18.670
Just tell him,
"I'm happy as long as you're alive".

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.970
- <i>Sure!</i>
- <i>We'll omit the countdown!</i>

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.750
Melord!

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.250
Have you lost control?!

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:32.480
<i>We've transferred our control</i>
<i>to the number three bridge!</i>

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.580
<i>We can avoid hitting the ground!</i>

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:35.450
Okay.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.320
How dare you hit the Melord!

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.900
Char, now! Go!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.560
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.840
Their shuttle's taken off!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.740
The Zeta and the Hyaku Shiki
must be in there!

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:10.950
It's useless.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.210
Good luck Char, Kamille.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.120
Whatever you do, don't die in vain.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.820
- Uncomfortable, aren't you?
- No.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.260
But I can never get used to...

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.360
...this terrible feeling.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:54.630
In the old days, people went out to space
enduring G-Forces many times stronger.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.100
Yes, I know.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:00.140
These people believed their
promised land existed in space.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:05.230
Rather than hate the elites on Earth
who forced them into space...

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.750
...they thought it more positive
to think that way.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.550
Once people were able
to shake off gravity...

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.590
...they acquired a new sense.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.090
And that led to the emergence
of Newtypes.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.660
In that regard, outer space was
indeed a promised land.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.090
That's easy to understand.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.100
I will also pursue that promise.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:29.270
Right now, that is my
responsibility.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:35.600
<i>Unless I do that, Four will</i>
<i>cease to live within me.</i>

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.690
- Did you see that?
- Yes. Likely flashes from a battle.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.350
It must be the Argama.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.190
Looks like we've reached orbit.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:57.530
Lieutenant!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.120
We'll prepare to support the Argama.
Come.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.000
Yes, sir!

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.320
Their defense is weaker than usual.
Perhaps a lack of supplies?

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:29.690
Batch, return to protect the Argama!

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.730
Roger!

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:33.430
Qum!

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.470
Qum!

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:39.360
- Fa!
- It'll be all right.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:42.570
Shinta, go to your room.
Play with Haro and stay there.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.740
- We'll be all right.
- I'm counting on you.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.540
Fa!

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.210
Fa's going out to fight.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.180
She has to fight, or else
the Argama will be gone!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.920
Kamille, are you all right?

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:00.790
Yes.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.020
The weight has now been reduced
considerably.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.530
Lieutenant, this can go, too!

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.200
- Hurry!
- Right!

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.030
- Ready?!
- Yes.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:21.440
You're using your vernier too much!
It's your final lifeline! Use it sparingly!

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.050
I'm sorry! I'll be more careful!

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.380
Oh, that can't go!

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.220
Why not?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.720
It's got gifts from Miss Beltorchika
for the crew of the Argama!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.950
I see.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.090
- Load it onto the Zeta!
- Right!

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:36.390
- We're starting the shuttle!
- Right!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.190
<i>Ready, Lieutenant!</i>

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.070
We have power to reach there?

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.100
How is our ascending angle?

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.760
We'll get there in about fifteen minutes.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.100
I hope the Argama will survive
until we get there.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.610
I'll disconnect the joints
securing the mobile suits!

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.580
Don't forget the spare oxygen cylinders
for our normal suits.

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.110
Yes, sir!

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:31.510
Second wave... no, third wave coming!

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.750
Forget the trivial details! Starboard!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.790
What's going on with
the anti-air battery?!

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:40.980
Portside gunners, barrage is weak!
What the hell are you doing?!

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.190
There are eight enemy mobile suits
out there! They're new models!

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.790
We still have the Methuss!

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:49.060
Gather the mobile suits
and have them protect the Argama!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.930
I can't allow it.
I don't want to damage the Methuss!

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:52.840
But I'm used to piloting the Methuss.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.510
The barrage is weak!
Shoot down at least one of them!

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.570
If your death will end this war,
I'll permit you to go.

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:00.740
Yes, sir!

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.050
- What's the matter?!
- <i>Captain Bright, is Fa there?!</i>

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.520
She's here. What's up?

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.410
<i>Those little kids. They're up to no good.</i>

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:10.520
- Hey, come out of there!
- What are you doing?!

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:13.390
- Can we open this from the outside?!
- It'll take time!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:14.920
Can you move it?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.830
I always watch, but...
Maybe like this.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.930
- <i>I'm telling you, come out!</i>
- <i>There's no way you can move this thing!</i>

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:23.560
They sound mad!

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.870
We'll be okay as long as we do it
like Kamille.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.370
Come on, kids!

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.010
<i>Is it this lever?</i>

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.050
<i>We should've brought Haro here with us.</i>

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:35.270
<i>Don't be silly!</i>
<i>We don't need toys in battle!</i>

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:37.340
- <i>But still...!</i>
- Those children!

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.180
Do they think they're Newtypes
or something?!

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.250
One of our Nemos has been destroyed!

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.220
<i>We must protect the Argama!</i>

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.080
- <i>In place of Kamille?!</i>
- <i>That's right!</i>

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.860
- <i>We're going to do it!</i>
- <i>Hurry and move it!</i>

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:50.460
Fa.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.070
Go to the Methuss and give those two
a spanking they won't forget!

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.860
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.530
Thank you, Captain Bright.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.880
I'm opening it!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.440
You two!

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.370
I've told you a million times
never to touch this!

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.780
- Get out at once!
- Okay.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.260
How are you feeling?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:29.060
The battleship that you belonged to
is now under attack.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.230
I'd like to hear your comments on this.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.640
Any decent human being
would find this unbearable.

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.410
I'm decent!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.450
That's why I came here!

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:41.410
You may say you've had
a change of heart...

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.410
...but we still see you as a spy.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.180
I find that quite regrettable!

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.690
What are your true objectives,
Ensign Reccoa?

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:50.810
I...

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.690
...I just didn't want to go against
what my heart feels.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.590
That's all.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.920
I don't believe you are
that ideological.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:01.230
My ideology is to comply with
what my heart feels!

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.730
Don't you understand that?

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.400
No, I don't.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.600
I'm selfish.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.300
And that's why you betrayed them?

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.240
Is that wrong?

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.040
Our patrol ship has been sunk!

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.370
Can't they survive until we
catch up to them?

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.380
Is the Yazan team able to launch
with the Hambrabis?!

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.420
Yes, sir!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.090
- Can we get there in time?
- I'm sure we will.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.960
I just saw some new flashes.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.130
They can hold for a while.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.060
I'm amazed. So, you can tell?

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.200
Well, it looks that way to me.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.020
What?!

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.750
Th-The output's increased?!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:13.710
Batch!

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.180
Lieutenant Apolly, are you all right?!

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:29.850
Thanks, Fa.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.990
- <i>Will we get there?</i>
- I don't know.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.030
- Let's go!
- <i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.870
Lieutenant!

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:48.160
I'll take you with the Zeta!

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:49.730
But then the Zeta won't make it!

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:52.010
Rather than go separately
and neither of us getting there...

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.050
...it would be better if at least
you got there, Lieutenant.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.410
All right!

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:06.450
<i>Fa, bail!</i>

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:07.490
Right.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:13.630
Y-You're kidding!

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.000
It's the Zeta Gundam and the Hyaku Shiki!

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:24.870
What?!

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.240
Have you confirmed it?!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.510
No mistake about it!

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:28.910
The barrage has got to be thicker!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.640
We'll pick up the Zeta and the Hyaku Shiki,
then return to the Moon!

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:32.690
Yes, sir!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.490
<i>Is it you, Fa?! Fa Yuiry!</i>

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:38.960
<i>Are you injured?!</i>

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:39.960
Kamille.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.650
Did you come out with the Methuss?!
Why?!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.900
I wanted to see for myself
just one more time...

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.760
...if I'm suited... to be a pilot.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:54.440
<i>Kamille, don't worry about me.</i>
<i>Go out and fight.</i>

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:03.750
Argama!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:05.790
Shoot out the Mega Bazooka Launcher!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:07.110
Do you hear me?!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.090
Lieutenant Quattro is requesting
the Mega Launcher!

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.790
- Give it to him!
- But what if the enemy shoots it down?!

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:14.690
Worry about that if it gets shot down!

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.830
Ready to shoot out!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.130
It's going!

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:29.130
You're not going to stop it!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.140
Where's the enemy ship?!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.150
Nemo team, spread out!
Otherwise, you'll get sucked into this!

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:47.990
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.400
Captain Gady!
Please have this ship pull back!

00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:58.800
What for?

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:01.840
It's the Mega Bazooka Launcher.
That thing's directed at this bridge!

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:04.730
I don't see anything!
Not even the Argama's main cannon...!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:08.680
Char and Kamille
have returned to this battle area!

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.180
Do you realize what that means?!

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.340
All right!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.320
Alexandria, retreat at top speed!

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:14.380
Yes, sir!

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:23.590
I won't let you fire it!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.060
Go down!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:37.210
It's just as you told us, Ensign Reccoa!

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.550
Hurry with the retreat!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.180
They can't fire again right away.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:43.220
We should also have
the mobile suits retreat.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:45.880
Good point, Ensign.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:53.220
How could I miss? Why?

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:56.720
I felt something get in the way.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.570
Will you explain it to me
so that I can understand?

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.870
All I can say is that I was drawn.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:06.910
To what?

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.940
To a strong man, like Yazan.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:12.980
Really.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:14.580
Excuse me.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:16.880
Damn.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.750
Ever since teaming with Scirocco,
I keep coming across strange ones.

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:22.720
- I'm glad that you're okay, Lt. Ramsus.
- Well, well.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.090
I hear you saved the Alexandria, Ensign.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.260
I wanted to prove I wasn't a spy.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.250
I know what your real target is.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:32.290
Scirocco's life, right?

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.490
Not a chance!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:38.760
I'm flattered with you overrating me,
but I'm not that great a soldier.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.540
Although it would be nice to attract
the attention of a man like that.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:46.000
It's the same thing!
So you're really that kind of woman.

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.270
Excuse me.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:50.280
No one's going to easily steal
the heart of that woman.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:52.680
Batch hasn't returned?!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.890
N-No.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:58.090
And I'm only alive
because you saved me, Fa.

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:00.480
Batch...!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:03.190
Lieutenant Apolly.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.860
What about you, Fa?

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:08.300
I know...
I had a close call, too.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.600
Fa!

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:11.940
But you know...

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:15.670
...those two tried to go out to fight
with the Methuss instead of me.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:17.640
Fa!

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.840
Then, I couldn't help...!

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:22.680
- Fa!
- That was very dangerous!

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:24.010
You two!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.020
I heard that you got an enemy mobile suit!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.820
You're really something, Fa!

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:28.920
Kamille!

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.010
- Job well done.
- Thank you very much, Captain Bright!

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:37.290
Thanks to you, I was able to avoid
becoming lost in space.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.330
You also saved us.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:41.170
You look well.

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:43.060
What are you being so shy about,
Lieutenant?

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:48.010
Well, I did take on that role
as a clown in Dakar.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.800
The broadcast was also aired
in the colonies.

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:52.670
A bootleg copy of the
original broadcast, that is.

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:56.340
Lieutenant, you've given Spacenoids hope.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.480
I look forward to
working with you...

00:21:58.550 --> 00:21:59.680
...Char Aznable.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:04.350
I feel the same way,
Captain Bright.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:21.870
But...

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:24.370
...Miss Reccoa cannot be alive.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:50.050
During a lull between battles,
Kamille meets Rosamia, Mineva...

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:54.390
...and Haman Karn at a colony resort.

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:57.970
Char stands aghast at the coincidence.

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:02.130
Does Kamille have a power
for attracting the enemy?

00:24:03.410 --> 00:24:07.450
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"By the Lake".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
By The Lake

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:11.050
You will see the tears of time.
